[EMITTER:LISL_INSTRUCTION_WRITER]
[TARGET:E2B_WORKER_01]
[ID: DOOMREMAKE_INIT_SPEC_01]

PURPOSE: Initialize DoomRemake project structure and establish LISL workspace sharding.

PROJECT_INFO:
- Name: DoomRemake
- Target Framework: .NET 9.0
- Type: Console Application (Multiplayer Ready)
- Platform: Windows API Integration with WAD File Support

DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE:
```
DoomRemake/
├── src/                    # Source code directory
│   ├── DoomRemake.csproj  # Project file (.NET 9.0)
│   ├── Program.cs         # Application entry point
│   └── Core/              # Core subsystems
│       ├── InputHooks.cs  # Windows API input capture (User32.dll)
│       ├── WadFileHandler.cs  # WAD lump reading utilities
│       └── WadLoader.cs   # Asset loading utilities
├── assets/                # Game assets directory
│   ├── wads/             # DOOM WAD files
│   ├── textures/         # Texture packs
│   └── sounds/           # Sound effects and music
├── docs/                  # Documentation
│   └── LISL_Specs/       # LISL protocol specifications
├── logs/                  # Runtime log directory
├── DMI/                   # Dev Manager Instructions (read-only for workers)
├── WOI/                   # Worker Order Instructions (output from DEV_MANAGER)
└── WOutput/               # Worker Output (exclusive write zone)

LISL_SHARDING_PROTOCOL:
- DMI/: High-level task definitions (DEV_MANAGER writes, workers read)
- WOI/: Sequential specification files with incremental counters
- WOutput/: Generated code and build artifacts from worker execution

WINDOWS_API_INTEGRATION:
1. InputHooks class implements User32.dll keyboard/mouse hooks
   - Captures key press/release events
   - Captures mouse clicks, movement, and wheel scrolling
   - Thread-safe hook management with proper initialization/shutdown

WAD_FILE_HANDLING:
1. WadFileHandler provides standard file I/O for WAD lumps
2. Supports PWAD/DOOM format magic numbers
3. Parses lump directory entries (name, size, file position)
4. Loads individual lumps by name with error handling

EXPECTED_OUTPUT_STATUS:
- Directory structure fully established
- .NET 9.0 project configured with proper dependencies
- Core subsystems implemented and functional
- LISL sharding protocol documented and active
- All files include [EMITTER] tags for tracking

HANDOFF_SIGNAL:
Worker should create Finished.md in WOutput/ upon completion to signal DEV_MANAGER_12B_QAT for verification.